1
00:00:00,230 --> 00:00:01,320
Why is the sky blue?

2
00:00:01,620 --> 00:00:04,080
The answer is hiding inside sunlight.

3
00:00:04,260 --> 00:00:06,000
Sunlight looks white, but it's really

4
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:07,500
every color of the rainbow traveling

5
00:00:08,240 --> 00:00:09,040
together.

6
00:00:09,270 --> 00:00:10,330
Each color is a wave.

7
00:00:10,330 --> 00:00:12,160
Red waves are long and lazy.

8
00:00:12,160 --> 00:00:14,400
Blue waves are short and choppy.

9
00:00:14,630 --> 00:00:17,040
When sunlight hits the air, tiny molecules

10
00:00:17,090 --> 00:00:19,380
bounce the short blue waves in every

11
00:00:19,400 --> 00:00:20,070
direction.

12
00:00:20,070 --> 00:00:22,390
The long red waves mostly pass straight

13
00:00:22,390 --> 00:00:23,110
through.

14
00:00:23,130 --> 00:00:25,170
Blue scatters about six times more than

15
00:00:25,490 --> 00:00:27,840
red, so blue reaches your eyes from every

16
00:00:27,840 --> 00:00:28,940
part of the sky.

17
00:00:28,940 --> 00:00:30,540
But here's the odd part.

18
00:00:30,540 --> 00:00:32,650
Violet scatters even more than blue, so

19
00:00:32,650 --> 00:00:34,240
why isn't the sky violet?

20
00:00:34,240 --> 00:00:36,320
The sun sends out less of it.

21
00:00:36,320 --> 00:00:38,750
The upper atmosphere absorbs some, and our

22
00:00:38,750 --> 00:00:40,640
eyes are less sensitive to it.

23
00:00:40,640 --> 00:00:42,950
At sunset light crosses far more air, the

24
00:00:42,950 --> 00:00:45,720
blue gets scattered away and red is what's

25
00:00:45,730 --> 00:00:46,280
left.

26
00:00:46,480 --> 00:00:49,090
Blue sky by day, red sky by evening, Same

27
00:00:49,090 --> 00:00:50,950
sunlight, different path.

28
